there is a mismatch hardware project modal appearing which should never appear.
  >> FIXED b7a6c99. Cause: our own hostname migration. ensureHardwareHostname renames
     highascg-nvidia-595 -> highascg7579, but isLikelySameMachine only compared hostnames,
     so the box stopped recognising its own saved projects (checked: 5 of your projects on
     disk still say "highascg-nvidia-595", live host is "highascg7579") -> sameMachine=false
     -> the boot suppression never fired -> modal every startup. Now matches on hardwareId,
     then MAC, then hostname, with a legacy-name rule for projects saved before hardwareId
     existed. Also records hardwareId+mac when saving from now on. NEEDS KIOSK RELOAD.

devices view is super slow
  >> PARTLY FIXED b7a6c99, investigation still running for the rest.
     Confirmed contributor: the CG orphan sweep fired 180 serialized AMCP commands on every
     start/reconnect (see the log below - CG 1-700..789 CLEAR, one every ~500ms = ~90s).
     Device View's polls queued behind all of it. Now 3 batched round-trips.
     A separate audit of the Device View's own polling + server probe cost is in progress.

on a test laptop these are the logs after restart
  >> The ~500ms gap between EVERY command in this log is not an AMCP pacer - there is no
     rate limiter anywhere in the send path (checked amcp-protocol/-client-transport/-batch).
     It is the Node event loop being starved, i.e. the laptop is CPU-bound. Two candidates
     visible in this very log, both config not code:
       - "Initialized OpenGL 4.6 Mesa 25.2.8 AMD" = integrated GPU, no NVIDIA on that box
       - 2 channels at 1080p5000 (50fps) with gpu_texture:false, "frame copied to host for
         rendering" + vsync. That is a full CPU readback of 1920x1080 fifty times a second,
         twice over, on integrated graphics.
     Suggest testing that laptop at 1080p2500 with one channel before blaming the app.
     I cannot measure that box from here - this is read off the log, not verified on it.

